{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Tight","lean:module:Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.TightNormed","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.FrechetShohat","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelConfluence"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.exists_subseq_tendsto_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.exists_subseq_tendsto_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L281-L307","doc":"**The composed conditional theorem (REP attack 2, MAIN).** The\nbalanced kernel family — probability measures on `[0,∞)` with all\nmoments finite and moments converging to `{k!}` — is TIGHT (proved: the\n`k = 2` moment convergence alone suffices, via Markov), hence under\nProkhorov selection a weakly convergent subsequence EXISTS, and under\nmoment passage + classical Carleman its limit — and the limit of every\nother convergent subsequence (`subseq_limit_eq_schwinger`) — IS the unit\nSchwinger measure. Archimedean (REP) holds for the constructed family\nwithout any fibre-level uniqueness input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.subseq_limit_eq_schwinger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.subseq_limit_eq_schwinger","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L249-L279","doc":"**Subsequential-limit identification (conditional).** Let `μs` be\nprobability measures on `[0,∞)` with all moments finite and `k`-th\nmoments converging to `k!`. Then — conditional on moment passage and the\nclassical Carleman theorem (whose divergence hypothesis for `{k!}` is\nLean-PROVED, `carlemanCondition_factorial`) — every weakly convergent\nsubsequence of `μs` has limit exactly the unit Schwinger measure\n`e^{−s}·ds`. Fibre-level uniqueness is never invoked: determinacy enters\nonly for the archimedean limit sequence `{k!}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes.hasStieltjesMoments_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes.hasStieltjesMoments_limit","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L236-L236","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes.mk","kind":"ctor","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L235-L235","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.MomentPassageStieltjes","kind":"class","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L225-L244","doc":"**Moment passage to weak limits (classical theorem, Mathlib gap).**\nIf probability measures on `[0,∞)`, with all moments finite and each\n`k`-th moment converging to `M k`, converge weakly to `μ`, then `μ`\nrealizes the moment data `M`. Classical proof: for each `k` the bounded\n`2k`-th moments give uniform integrability of `s ↦ s^k`, so the moment\nfunctional passes to the weak limit (Billingsley, *Probability and\nMeasure*, 3rd ed., Thm 25.12, and the proof of Thm 30.2). This is the\n\"moments of the limit\" half of Fréchet–Shohat, separated from selection.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.Probability.MomentProblem` (new file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal.exists_subseq_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal.exists_subseq_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L218-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.ProkhorovSelectionReal","kind":"class","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L209-L223","doc":"**Prokhorov/Helly selection (classical theorem, Mathlib gap).** A\ntight sequence of Borel probability measures on `ℝ` has a subsequence\nconverging in the topology of weak convergence. Direct half of\nProkhorov's theorem (Prokhorov 1956, Thm 1.12; Billingsley, *Convergence\nof Probability Measures*, 2nd ed., Thm 5.1). The pinned Mathlib carries\nthe tightness definitions (`IsTightMeasureSet`) and the Lévy–Prokhorov\nmetrizability of weak convergence, but not the compactness theorem.\n\nTODO upstream: `Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Prokhorov` (new file). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.isTightMeasureSet_of_tendsto_integral_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.isTightMeasureSet_of_tendsto_integral_sq","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L182-L194","doc":"**Convergent second moments ⇒ tight (the balanced-kernel form).**\nA sequence of Borel probability measures on `ℝ` whose second moments\nconverge (for the balanced family: `∫ s² ∂K_n = N^bal_{q_n}(3) → 2! = 2`\n— an exact identity, `N^bal(3) = 2 + (√q−1)²/√q`) is tight. Tightness of\nthe constructed family is thus *nearly free*: bounded second moment +\nMarkov, no kernel-specific tail estimate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.exists_forall_le_of_tendsto","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.exists_forall_le_of_tendsto","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L174-L180","doc":"A convergent real sequence is bounded above — the uniform-bound step\nfor a family whose second moments converge (Mathlib's\n`Filter.Tendsto.bddAbove_range`, unpacked to an explicit bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.isTightMeasureSet_of_integral_sq_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.isTightMeasureSet_of_integral_sq_le","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L147-L172","doc":"**Uniform second moment ⇒ tight.** A family of Borel probability\nmeasures on `ℝ` with a single bound `∫ s² ∂(μs i) ≤ C` for every `i` is\ntight: the compact windows `[−R, R]` catch mass `≥ 1 − C/R²` of every\nmember simultaneously (Markov), and `C/R² → 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.measure_compl_closedBall_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.measure_compl_closedBall_le","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L126-L143","doc":"The Markov tail bound in `ℝ≥0∞`, against the complement of the\ncompact window `[−R, R] = Metric.closedBall 0 R` — the shape consumed by\nMathlib's tightness API. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.tail_measureReal_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BalancedKernelTightness.tail_measureReal_le","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BalancedKernelTightness.lean#L98-L124","doc":"**Markov tail bound from the second moment.** A finite Borel measure\non `ℝ` with second moment `∫ s² ∂μ ≤ C` puts mass at most `C/R²` outside\n`(−R, R)`: `μ.real {s | R ≤ |s|} ≤ C/R²`. This is\n`mul_meas_ge_le_integral_of_nonneg` applied to `f = s²` at level `R²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}